# What must not leave this machine.
#
# `railway up` uploads the working directory to Railway's build servers. It is
# not a git push: files that .gitignore excludes from the repository can still
# be in the build context, and there is no reason for a hosting provider's
# build machine to receive funding strategy, investor applications, or notes
# from conversations with users.
#
# These are the same documents .gitignore already keeps out of the repo. Listing
# them again here is deliberate duplication — the two mechanisms are
# independent, and the one that matters is the one that runs.

# ── Private documents ──
SESSION_CONTEXT.md
CONVERSATION_HISTORY.md
USER_CONVERSATIONS.md
SOUL.md
FUNDING_PATH.md
FUNDING_OPTIONS.md
OFFICE_PLAN.md
REALISTIC_OUTCOME.md
DAILY_PLAYBOOK.md
DAILY_REALITY_CHECK.md
YC_*.md
AGENTIC_MARKET_SUBMISSION.md
INTEGRATION_PLAYBOOK.md
/private/

# ── Added 2026-09-22, after `.dockerignore` was found to have the same gap ──
#
# `railway up` sends the working directory, not the git tree, so anything
# `.gitignore` excludes still leaves the machine unless it is named here too.
# This file and `.dockerignore` are the two independent mechanisms, and both
# had drifted from the list they were meant to mirror.
#
# `.env` was the sharp one: it holds HALDIR_ENCRYPTION_KEY, the master key for
# the vault, and `.dockerignore` has always excluded it while this file did
# not.
.env
.env.*
.mcpregistry_*
drafts/
.aider*
.drafts/
.aws/
.ssh/
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

